-- title:
--   The maximum norm is invariant under negation
-- statement:
--   For every $x \in \mathbb{R}^d$,
--   $$\|-x\|_\infty \;=\; \|x\|_\infty,
--   \qquad\text{where}\quad \|x\|_\infty = \sup_i |x_i| .$$
--
--   The evenness of the maximum norm; combined with additivity of coordinates it gives the symmetry $\|x-y\|_\infty = \|y-x\|_\infty$, which is what makes cube-based distance conditions symmetric in their two arguments.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The lemma is marked `@[simp]`, so the rewrite is applied automatically by simplification.
